  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Harishankar Rampravesh Singh vs State Of Maharashtra on 7 June, 2024 P.H. Jayani 03 aba1518.2024.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1518 Of 2024 Harishankar Rampravesh Singh .... Applicant V/s. The State of Maharashtra .... Respondent Mr. Nehal Desale for the Applicant. Mr. Mayur Sonavane, App for the State. Ms. Sneha Solanke, Psi, Uttan Sagari Police Station, present. Coram: Shyam C. Chandak, J. Dated : 07th June, 2024. P.C. :- 1) The Applicant is apprehending his arrest in F.I.R. bearing Crime No.22/2021, under Sections 328 read with 34 of the Indian Penal Code and Sections 4 and 58 of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 registered with Uttan Sagari Police Station, Mira-Bhayandar, Vasai Virar Police Commissionerate on 29/01/2021. 2) Heard Mr. Desale, learned Advocate for the Applicant and Mr. Sonavane, learned APP for the State. Harishankar Rampravesh Singh vs State Of Maharashtra on 7 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/93001365/ 1 5)",
    "facts": "On inquiry, he disclosed that, it was procured by his brother/co-accused Naushad Khan from the present Applicant. As such, there is a prima facie case of a serious offence against the Applicant.",
    "arguments": "3) Learned Advocate for the Applicant submitted that, neither the Applicant is figured in the FIR nor the investigating material transpired his role in the alleged crime. Thus, the Applicant is not directly or indirectly involved in the offence. Therefore, ad-interim protection may be granted to the Applicant."
  },
